    "narrative": "With the 2026 season winding down, Ghost Ride the WHIP faces a condensed slate, forcing us to lean heavily on efficiency as we chase points in the SB and AVG categories. **Brice Turang** earns the nod today with a 59.1 efficiency score against Peralta, F. While Peralta, F remains a formidable arm, **Brice Turang** benefits from a high-leverage spot in the order and a park factor that marginally stabilizes his expected outcome. He remains our primary engine for stolen bases given the current absence of **Corbin Carroll** and **Jose Caballero**, who are unfortunately sidelined by a team off-day. We are closely monitoring the lineup status of **Seiya Suzuki** and **Giancarlo Stanton**; if either shifts down in the order, their efficiency scores will likely drop below our 40-point floor, prompting a pivot to **Mickey Moniak** or **Trevor Story** to chase speed and secondary upside.\n\nThe bench decision process today was dominated by the lack of viable alternatives, as **Josh Naylor**, **James Wood**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, and **Tyler Soderstrom** are all currently inactive. Among the remainder of our deep bench, **Max Muncy** came closest to cracking the lineup due to his career BvP against today's projected opposing starters, but he ultimately yielded to the defensive flexibility and high-contact profiles of our middle infielders. Looking ahead, we are tracking the development of prospects **Travis Bazzana**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Cole Young** alongside **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Moises Ballesteros**, **Dalton Rushing**, and **Griffin Conine**. We must be vigilant with our game caps; should weather reports deteriorate at any of the active sites, we will immediately bench any player with a score under 50 to preserve our remaining eligibility for a more favorable tomorrow.",
